            <ArticleTitle>Cardiac arrest during dipyridamole imaging.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1103-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of cardiac arrest and subsequent acute myocardial infarction occurring during thallium-201 imaging with oral dipyridamole augmentation is presented. Previous reports emphasizing the safety of this procedure are briefly reviewed and a recommendation for close hemodynamic and arrhythmia monitoring during the study is made. Large doses of oral dipyridamole may be contraindicated in patients with unstable angina.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
